{{- /*
The running footer Chrome draws on every printed page.

Chrome renders header and footer templates in an ISOLATED context: the page's
own stylesheet does not reach here and the inherited font-size is zero, so
every property has to be inline and absolute. Sizes are in px for the same
reason -- pt and mm are not honoured in this context.

"pageNumber" and "totalPages" are Chrome's own substitution classes; it fills
their contents in as it lays each page out.

The horizontal padding matches the page margin, because the footer is drawn
outside the page box and would otherwise sit flush against the paper edge.
*/ -}}
<div style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0 {{ .MarginCSS }};
            font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 8px;
            color: #5b6470; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
  <span>{{ .Doc.ProductName }}{{ with .Doc.DocumentVersion }} &middot; Version {{ . }}{{ end }}</span>
  <span>Page <span class="pageNumber"></span> of <span class="totalPages"></span></span>
</div>
